" ⠿ overbrainer   1 Project  2 Dataset  3 Pipeline  4 Training  5 Logs  6 Compare                            rust_expert "
"╭ data ──────────────────────────────────────────────╮╭ question ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮"
"│ ▼ ownership  2 sub, 5 q, 4 a                       ││ What happens to a borrow when the owner is moved?              │"
"│   ▼ Borrowing  3 q, 2 a                            ││                                                                │"
"│       [a] What happens to a borrow when the owner  ││ id 0a40…e3d3  answered, usable                                 │"
"│       [x] Why can't a &mut and a & borrow coexist? ││                                                                │"
"│       [ ] When does NLL end a borrow?              ││ model deepseek-r1  in 312  out 1840                            │"
"│   ▶ Lifetimes  1 q, 1 a                            ││ finish stop  reasoning raw                                     │"
"│   ▶ (missing subtopic)  1 q, 1 a                   ││ ── reasoning ──                                                │"
"│   traits  0 sub, 0 q, 0 a                          ││ Let me think about what a move does to a borrow.               │"
"│ ▶ old_topic (not configured)  1 sub, 1 q, 1 a      ││ The borrow checker tracks every live reference to the owner.   │"
"│                                                    ││ A move invalidates the owner's place, so no borrow may outlive │"
"│                                                    ││ it.                                                            │"
"│                                                    ││ ── answer ──                                                   │"
"│                                                    ││ The borrow must end before the move.                           │"
"│                                                    ││ If a reference is still used after the move, the compiler      │"
"│                                                    ││ reports E0505: cannot move out of the value because it is      │"
"│                                                    ││ borrowed.                                                      │"
"│                                                    ││ Non-lexical lifetimes end a borrow at its last use, not at the │"
"│                                                    ││ end of its scope, so many such programs compile.               │"
"│                                                    ││                                                                │"
